#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# cot

#% text
# `cot(x)` gives the cotangent 1/tan(x).

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `cot(x)` stays unevaluated for symbolic `x`; where `tan(x)` has an exact value, `cot(x)` is its reciprocal.

#% item
# Machine numbers, balls and complex numbers give numerical values.

#% item
# `cot` is listable.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
cot(pi/4)
#% output
#= 1

#% cell
cot(1.0)
#% output
#= 0.6420926159343306

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# Symbolic arguments and symmetry:

#% cell
cot(-x)
#% output
#= -cot(x)

#% text
# 30 digits:

#% cell
n(cot(1), 30)
#% output
#= 0.6420926159343307030064199865942656

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `tan`, `sin`, `cos`, `tan`
